# 24. HUMAN VOICE STANDARD

Human voices must improve interpretation.

Do not append names simply to make the note look researched.

Use human evidence when it explains:

- why a sector moved;
- why a stock reacted unexpectedly;
- what positioning may have mattered;
- what investors think is priced;
- why two professionals interpret the same evidence differently;
- how a medium-term SPX target is constructed.

Prefer a smaller number of relevant voices over a long quote dump.

